  ('63ed2515-ec96-5588-93fb-b019554a51a7','7c91189d-f5e8-5fd8-ba49-50eb20f62d64',1,'A','Exactly 8 lines must be drawn for each charge'),
  ('1be8ac78-08a3-5a2b-95fb-5c58927de8cb','7c91189d-f5e8-5fd8-ba49-50eb20f62d64',1,'B','The number of lines is fixed by Coulomb''s law'),
  ('9d999374-493d-5a9e-bba4-bafd98d50e74','7c91189d-f5e8-5fd8-ba49-50eb20f62d64',1,'C','The number of lines is not important; relative density is what matters'),
  ('ecdcc2af-26ae-579a-8429-46dd0ceab3e8','7c91189d-f5e8-5fd8-ba49-50eb20f62d64',1,'D','More lines always mean a stronger field regardless of area'),
  ('2613e901-185f-579d-b3ea-4c86ee05de9e','96c645c5-7a22-5143-871b-f1cb23a76877',1,'A','Because field lines are only two-dimensional'),
  ('2d125418-b755-5e76-bd2e-cbc06165cf59','96c645c5-7a22-5143-871b-f1cb23a76877',1,'B','Because we live in three dimensions and the figure is drawn on paper in 2D'),
  ('6097ca9a-841c-5f58-9349-d59ae462a827','96c645c5-7a22-5143-871b-f1cb23a76877',1,'C','Because cross-sectional area is easier to calculate'),
  ('67293eb4-ee2a-5d6a-a1a1-6e1c8f2fb3d9','96c645c5-7a22-5143-871b-f1cb23a76877',1,'D','Because field lines are always perpendicular to the surface'),
  ('7418f0f4-23a1-5b2e-be09-c5e888fc3d81','3d6ae8de-896e-5330-8011-47652756f3d3',1,'A','Because the field strength is constant at all distances'),
  ('bafac6c5-ca79-50c8-a273-916fe856b360','3d6ae8de-896e-5330-8011-47652756f3d3',1,'B','Because the electric field decreases as 1/r^2 while the area increases as r^2'),
  ('3d898a19-e8a3-59b8-9ebc-98c7bab9c22f','3d6ae8de-896e-5330-8011-47652756f3d3',1,'C','Because the charge itself changes with distance'),
  ('57bef2cc-af3b-553b-a448-f12919b4ab2b','3d6ae8de-896e-5330-8011-47652756f3d3',1,'D','Because field lines cannot be created or destroyed'),
  ('f5a8c6c9-e29a-52dd-8ddf-fe566d1d07c5','f9d2f9e7-25fe-58c3-ab07-b7b0ccd62cdb',1,'A','ΔΩ = ΔS * r^2'),
  ('b14355a7-758d-5efa-94f5-7bde2c27c997','f9d2f9e7-25fe-58c3-ab07-b7b0ccd62cdb',1,'B','ΔΩ = ΔS / r'),
  ('08c7f8d0-0629-5ff7-a6b4-73fb0f54a556','f9d2f9e7-25fe-58c3-ab07-b7b0ccd62cdb',1,'C','ΔΩ = ΔS / r^2'),
  ('77b70110-a8e3-576c-b348-fd0a47d43127','f9d2f9e7-25fe-58c3-ab07-b7b0ccd62cdb',1,'D','ΔΩ = r^2 / ΔS'),
  ('2862dbfd-f26f-5de7-b8da-63d5a48aa084','b692fa35-7af2-5e63-93b9-6305ab84c4f8',1,'A','E1/E2 = r1/r2'),
  ('751f6b0b-410f-520a-acb4-ac4ff8f4fd49','b692fa35-7af2-5e63-93b9-6305ab84c4f8',1,'B','E1/E2 = r2/r1'),
  ('b25d009a-84ce-5a52-b64e-e258a82cffac','b692fa35-7af2-5e63-93b9-6305ab84c4f8',1,'C','E1/E2 = r2^2/r1^2'),
  ('85b75a30-f95a-5ffc-9993-42bda5dd509c','b692fa35-7af2-5e63-93b9-6305ab84c4f8',1,'D','E1/E2 = r1^2/r2^2'),
  ('eff76422-5c65-502f-9be1-9ede4813386b','ff3f575c-8e41-5eb7-b5d6-819430af8cf6',1,'A','Coulomb, called them force vectors'),
  ('145ab3db-b8ed-5b60-aec4-a4755c63343a','ff3f575c-8e41-5eb7-b5d6-819430af8cf6',1,'B','Newton, called them gravitational lines'),
  ('37baf651-3739-5ece-b0aa-c18048eda2f0','ff3f575c-8e41-5eb7-b5d6-819430af8cf6',1,'C','Faraday, called them lines of force'),
  ('4b15df92-ac93-56cb-b18b-d2a4caf3e8af','ff3f575c-8e41-5eb7-b5d6-819430af8cf6',1,'D','Maxwell, called them electromagnetic waves'),
  ('a20ff452-6642-5d39-aff4-391d8db2f069','c64609dd-16f0-5239-8470-1223ca4be168',1,'A','It is a straight line in one dimension'),
  ('717e36b0-6637-5f5f-a5fd-0050e2f6f180','c64609dd-16f0-5239-8470-1223ca4be168',1,'B','It is a curve confined to a plane (two-dimensional)'),
  ('c07eb298-4cd3-5416-b2a1-e7e75bf85df5','c64609dd-16f0-5239-8470-1223ca4be168',1,'C','It is a space curve existing in three dimensions'),
  ('8a6d712c-01eb-55b4-8620-46052b1811dc','c64609dd-16f0-5239-8470-1223ca4be168',1,'D','It has no physical dimension, being purely conceptual'),
  ('d57bd7a4-9bc1-5a28-811c-73ad30aa8d65','a08ee205-ebc0-562f-988a-69a89d02e203',1,'A','By taking the scalar sum of all individual electric fields'),
  ('05f7681e-0c89-5bef-8a60-847a72117aad','a08ee205-ebc0-562f-988a-69a89d02e203',1,'B','By taking the vector sum of electric fields due to individual charges'),
  ('f83de1de-06aa-5eb5-977d-1ff5e34e474a','a08ee205-ebc0-562f-988a-69a89d02e203',1,'C','By multiplying all individual electric fields'),
  ('fa3b5ce6-28ba-59cf-8b18-da07a3e0645d','a08ee205-ebc0-562f-988a-69a89d02e203',1,'D','By taking the average of all individual electric fields'),
  ('aa091925-dc32-566a-a867-2cf223d3d747','dc658415-2c73-53fe-b2d8-0d65b94f5917',1,'A','E1 = (1/4πε0)(q1/r1P) * r̂1P'),
  ('5e9b10f7-bca2-5180-ae12-18c05ebe2641','dc658415-2c73-53fe-b2d8-0d65b94f5917',1,'B','E1 = (1/4πε0)(q1/r1P²) * r̂1P'),
  ('c9536850-3a0b-5019-8c84-b87b84830a4e','dc658415-2c73-53fe-b2d8-0d65b94f5917',1,'C','E1 = (1/4πε0)(q1*r1P²) * r̂1P'),
  ('60cc54a3-1f8d-5ac4-b6a1-b62f6c03d27f','dc658415-2c73-53fe-b2d8-0d65b94f5917',1,'D','E1 = (1/4πε0)(q1/r1P³) * r̂1P'),
  ('1ac7b32d-9fd9-5f1f-a7fc-7733b2d25da0','574f9364-0d64-5446-b931-2465021f8554',1,'A','A unit vector from point P to charge q1'),
  ('36ca7c4b-503c-548f-9b43-79d1c13e1d32','574f9364-0d64-5446-b931-2465021f8554',1,'B','A unit vector from charge q1 to point P'),
  ('762d1f57-a423-534d-adb8-d76c7bfae4ed','574f9364-0d64-5446-b931-2465021f8554',1,'C','A unit vector perpendicular to the line joining q1 and P'),
  ('3b28536a-9b77-555e-9973-c81091ae44a7','574f9364-0d64-5446-b931-2465021f8554',1,'D','The magnitude of the distance between q1 and P'),
  ('9d30881b-f341-5806-9e43-9ee88c1bef5b','54d2d74d-4838-5af7-aa5c-982ce3f2447d',1,'A','E(r) = (1/4πε0) * Σ(qi*riP²) * r̂iP'),
  ('3a4ecc4b-633d-5240-a8a4-470a9b6c30f4','54d2d74d-4838-5af7-aa5c-982ce3f2447d',1,'B','E(r) = (1/4πε0) * Σ(qi/riP) * r̂iP'),
  ('06bba3d6-fa5a-5d76-8b53-62dd7cb1d159','54d2d74d-4838-5af7-aa5c-982ce3f2447d',1,'C','E(r) = (1/4πε0) * Σ(qi/riP²) * r̂iP'),
